<AppPage
  title="Privacy Policy — claude-mcp"
  description="Privacy policy for claude-mcp and consiglio.fyi."
  current="privacy"
>
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="lede">Effective 23 September 2026</p>

  <p>This policy covers <a href="/claude-mcp/">claude-mcp</a> (“the app”), a personal Google OAuth client
    operated by Gabriele Consiglio (“I”, “me”), and the website consiglio.fyi.</p>

  <h2>Who uses the app</h2>
  <p>The app is for my personal use only, with Google accounts that I own. It is not offered to the public.</p>

  <h2>Google user data the app accesses</h2>
  <p>When I sign in with one of my Google accounts, the app requests these permissions:</p>
  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Service</th><th>Scopes</th><th>Used to</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Account</td>
          <td><code>openid</code>, <code>userinfo.email</code>, <code>userinfo.profile</code></td>
          <td>Identify which of my accounts is signed in.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Calendar</td>
          <td><code>calendar</code>, <code>calendar.events</code>, <code>calendar.readonly</code></td>
          <td>List calendars and events, check availability, create and update events.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Drive</td>
          <td><code>drive</code>, <code>drive.file</code>, <code>drive.readonly</code></td>
          <td>Search, read and create files.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Gmail</td>
          <td><code>gmail.readonly</code>, <code>gmail.modify</code>, <code>gmail.compose</code>, <code>gmail.send</code>, <code>gmail.labels</code>, <code>gmail.settings.basic</code></td>
          <td>Search and read messages, draft and send email, manage labels.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>How the data is used</h2>
  <p>Google user data is accessed only when I ask Claude Code to perform a task, and only to perform that task.
    It is not used for advertising, profiling, or any purpose other than the feature I requested.</p>

  <h2>Where the data goes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>On my computer.</strong> OAuth tokens are stored locally on my Mac, in files readable only by my user account.
      The app has no server and keeps no copy of my data anywhere else.</li>
    <li><strong>To Anthropic.</strong> Results returned by Google APIs are passed to Claude, the AI model behind Claude Code,
      as part of the conversation in which I requested them. Anthropic processes that content under its own
      <a href="https://www.anthropic.com/legal/privacy">privacy policy</a> and terms.</li>
    <li><strong>Nobody else.</strong> Google user data is not sold, rented or shared with any other third party.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Google API Services User Data Policy</h2>
  <p>The app’s use and transfer of information received from Google APIs adheres to the
    <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>,
    including the Limited Use requirements. In particular, Google user data is not used to develop, improve or train
    generalized AI or machine learning models, and no human reads it except me.</p>

  <h2>Retention and deletion</h2>
  <p>The app stores only OAuth tokens. To remove access, revoke claude-mcp at
    <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions">myaccount.google.com/permissions</a>
    and delete the local token files. Data in Google services stays in those services under Google’s control.</p>

  <h2>This website</h2>
  <p>consiglio.fyi is a static site hosted on GitHub Pages. It sets no cookies and runs no analytics.
    GitHub may log visitors’ IP addresses for security; see the
    <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub Privacy Statement</a>.
    Fonts are loaded from Google Fonts.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>If this policy changes, the new version is published on this page with a new effective date.</p>
</AppPage>
